  "body": "Found during #3129 (PR #3167).\n\n## What happens\nRotary Offset with strategy Zigzag or Auto plans each developed level with `machining3d::hsm::plan_level`, with a seam. The level gets Zigzag rows only. A row touches a shoulder wall or an island only at its ends. A cusp can stay between each two ends, as in #3129.\n\nPR #3167 adds closing rings to the 3D pocket levels. It does not add them to the wrap levels (`seam.is_some()`). The developed area of a wrap level ends at the seam. A ring on each boundary loop also follows the two seam edges of the strip. These two edges are one physical line, so the ring cuts that line two times.\n\n## Expected\nThe Zigzag rows of a wrap level close with a ring on each wall and island. The ring does not follow the seam edges of the developed strip.\n\n## Notes\n- `crates/app/tests/rotary_verify.rs::a_rough_over_an_oversized_bar_peels_from_the_stock_radius` pins the move count of the matching bar (2064). A full ring on the developed area gave 2863 moves.\n- First, measure the shoulder cusp on a wrap level with rows only. If there is no cusp, close this issue with the reading.\n\n## Done means\nA pin measures the shoulder or island wall of a Rotary Offset Zigzag level. It fails before the change and passes after it. The crossing check and the rotary verify stay clean.\n",
